## Review Requirements

- All changes require at least one approval from a code owner
- Code owners are responsible for:
  - Reviewing pull requests for their areas
  - Ensuring changes follow architecture patterns
  - Verifying security and performance implications
  - Maintaining test coverage

## Emergency Bypass

In case of critical security fixes or production incidents, the repository owner may bypass code owner approval with documented justification.

## Adding New Owners

To add new code owners:
1. Update this file with the new owner and their areas
2. Ensure the new owner understands their responsibilities
3. Document the change in the changelog